target:    admin/index.php
gate:      php tests/degradation-notice-honesty-test.php
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    does not read the recorded severity
rationale: Stop reading the severity the call site recorded and hard-code LOAD, which silently routes every operational record back into the red "reinstall the plugin" notice while leaving the two-notice structure standing. This is the shape the first fix took - severity reconstructed renderer-side - and it is worth pinning because it looks correct: the warning branch is still there, it is just unreachable. A gate that only checked the branch existed would pass.
---
--- a/admin/index.php
+++ b/admin/index.php
@@ -4195,7 +4195,7 @@
             // at runtime. record_degradation() is told which it is at the catch block that
             // knows. Legacy records written before that parameter existed default to LOAD,
             // which is what they all were; they age out within DEGRADATION_TTL anyway.
-            $severity = isset($record['severity']) ? (string) $record['severity'] : wp_slimstat::DEGRADATION_LOAD;
+            $severity = wp_slimstat::DEGRADATION_LOAD;
 
             if (wp_slimstat::DEGRADATION_OPERATIONAL === $severity) {
                 $operational_items .= $item;
